globalThis.pzCourseExport="# Adenosyl B12 · course dossier\n\nRevision: Revision 92\ncourse:6fc75e7f-06dc-53dc-bfe2-63d6a0ffcb32\ndocumented_course\n2025-12-10 · Off by 2026-10-21 · Patient review associates the October 21 B12 depletion with this earlier adenosyl B12 course. Course is closed by that date, not a witnessed last dose. The October diary did not identify the preparation; later unspecified-form B12 use does not demonstrate uninterrupted adenosyl dosing.\nDate-window anchor: Recorded course start · 2025-12-10\n\n## Baseline before the selected anchor\n\n- 2025-11-04 · More laptop tolerance with dimming, red filter and pacing · Despite occasional crashes he described being at his usual baseline on November 4. By November 21 he reported managing a dimmed/red laptop through the day by pacing passive media and some chatting. He contrasted this with immediate PEM from turning over in bed at the earlier winter nadir. · preceding winter most severely impaired state · Adaptive equipment and task selection changed what he could tolerate. This does not establish comparable capacity for work, ordinary screens or unpaced activity.\n  Source · baseline_states:BL-21\n\n## Intended targets\n\nNo linked record at this scope.\n\n## Actions and doses\n\n- 2025-12-10 · Start\n  Source · 2025-12-10 · start · inferred diary day · reported_use · primary · S2:3720–3720 · [intervention_events:S2-L03720-E1]\n\n## Course timing evidence\n\n- 2026-10-21 · stopped by · Patient-reviewed off-by bound; October source confirms B12 depletion but does not identify the B12 formulation or exact final dose.\n  Source · intervention_events:S2-L08761-E1\n- 2026-11-20 · stopped by · Confirmed off the regimen by this date. Exact last dose unknown.\n  Source · pz_regimen_snapshot:PZ-STACK-2026-11-20\n- 2026-11-23 · course review · The reviewer tentatively associates the October 21 report of running out of B12 some days earlier with this December adenosyl B12 course. The October entry gives no form. May 9 refers to depleted methyl B12 capsules and May 23 records a genuine restart with unspecified form. Whether that restart used the December product is unresolved.\n  Source · pz_review57_course:course:6fc75e7f-06dc-53dc-bfe2-63d6a0ffcb32\n\n## Potential effects\n\nNo linked record at this scope.\n\n## Potential effects reported outside a specific course\n\nNo linked record at this scope.\n\n## Intervention product links (course attribution unverified)\n\n- Life Extension · B12 Elite · https://www.iherb.com/pr/life-extension-b12-elite-60-vegetarian-lozenges-1-000-mcg-per-lozenge/114465 · Adenosylcobalamin is one of two labeled forms. The historical isolated adenosyl B12 course has no confirmed brand.\n  Source · User-supplied product link\n\n## Source evidence and qualifications\n\n- [archive_messages:S1-M59821] · reported 2025-11-04T17:23:43+01:00 · i'm dong ok (at baseline) now. woke at 1.30 pm (slept at 6am, sadly due to yesterday's crash I reversed my circadian cycle again sigh) · patient message · 2025-11-04T17:23:43+01:00\n- [archive_messages:S1-M61729] · reported 2025-11-21T14:22:13+01:00 · mostly not much has changed in the past year, i'm just a littel more able to do stuff (for which i'm grateful), but i think this is in large part due to two things, after initial improvement compared to last winter's very severe state (turning around in bed →immediate corrosive pem): 1/ installing software on laptop that drastically dims brightness and adds a red tinted overlay →suddenly was able to use laptop all day without crashing unlike before when the blue brightness crashed me almost immediately 2/ learning what activities i can do to keep dopamine constantly engaged but not push myself over energy budget (so mostly passive consumption sadly and some chatting) · patient message · 2025-11-21T14:22:13+01:00\n- [baseline_states:BL-21] · 2025-11-04 · through 2025-11-21 · More laptop tolerance with dimming, red filter and pacing · Despite occasional crashes he described being at his usual baseline on November 4. By November 21 he reported managing a dimmed/red laptop through the day by pacing passive media and some chatting. He contrasted this with immediate PEM from turning over in bed at the earlier winter nadir. · preceding winter most severely impaired state · Adaptive equipment and task selection changed what he could tolerate. This does not establish comparable capacity for work, ordinary screens or unpaced activity.\n- [intervention_events:S2-L03720-E1] · 2025-12-10 · reported 2025-12-10 · Adenosyl B12 · start · inferred diary day · reported_use · primary\n- [intervention_events:S2-L08761-E1] · reported 2026-10-21 · Vitamin B12 (form unspecified) · ran_out_earlier_unspecified · Patient wrote \"some days ago, unsure when exactly\". · inferred diary day · omission_or_hold · primary\n- [source_lines:S2:3720] · changes: start adenosyl b12\n- [treatment_intervals:S2-I-S2-L03720-E1] · 2025-12-10 · Adenosyl B12 · 2025-12-10 · end_not_documented_current_use_unknown · Start/use documented. No confirmed end; current use unknown. · primary";
